NAME
    edtest - ed25519 on-target check and measurement

SYNOPSIS
    edtest

DESCRIPTION
    Runs the RFC 8032 test vectors for the ed25519 crate on this machine, and
    measures the two things a host test cannot answer: how much stack a
    signature costs, and how long one takes.

    The vectors are the published ones, so a disagreement between this machine
    and the host build shows up as a disagreement about a value neither of them
    invented.

    The stack figure is only printed when the probe has been CALIBRATED: the
    same measurement is run around a function with a known extra 4KB frame and
    must read about 4KB higher. A probe that silently measured nothing would
    otherwise report a small, plausible number.

    Timings are measured with the monotonic clock. Under QEMU they are emulated
    and pessimistic against real hardware by roughly an order of magnitude, so
    read them as a ceiling.

EXIT STATUS
    0   every check passed
    1   a vector failed, or the stack probe did not calibrate

SEE ALSO
    selftest - the relocating-loader regression check
